    "title" "Extra Shape Parts"
    "description" "[h1]Extra Shape Parts[/h1]
shapez 2 has four shape quadrant types: circle, square, windmill and star. This mod adds ten more, and puts them on the map so they can be mined rather than only built.

[h2]The shapes[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Gear[/b] - two square teeth per quadrant, eight around the shape
[*][b]Cross[/b] - a square bitten at the corner, so four make a plus
[*][b]Diamond[/b] - a whole diamond in each quadrant, four making a checkerboard
[*][b]Dome[/b] - a half disc that turns one way
[*][b]Wedge[/b] - a thin triangle that turns the other
[*][b]Leaf[/b] - a pointed lens along the diagonal
[*][b]Flower[/b] - four petals with a waist between them
[*][b]Sawblade[/b] - three raked teeth per quadrant
[*][b]Bar[/b] - one arm of a cross, on its own
[*][b]Dot[/b] - a whole circle floating in its quadrant
[/list]

They cut, stack, paint, crystallise and rotate exactly like the vanilla four, because the game's shape operations never look at which part they are holding. Nothing new to learn.

[h2]Side quests[/h2]
Seven new chains in the research screen's Side Quests tab, twenty-six goals in all. Each chain starts with one production line and every step adds one thing to the factory that built the step before it - a colour, a stacker, a pin pusher, a crystal generator - so no step asks you to start again.

[h2]Hexagonal mode[/h2]
Every shape is built for the mode it is used in: a 90 degree quadrant in the standard game and a 60 degree sector in hexagonal mode, with its own mesh. The side quests adapt too. Both are supported.

[h2]Where they come from[/h2]
Gear, Cross, Diamond, Dome and Wedge are [b]rare[/b]; Bar, Dot, Sawblade, Flower and Leaf are [b]very rare[/b]. They turn up in shape patches on the map, in the map resource filter, and in randomly generated research goals - anywhere the game asks for a shape.

Every shape is designed around one constraint: a stacked layer covers the inner three quarters of the layer below, so whatever tells two shapes apart has to sit in the outer rim. These do.

[h2]Before you install[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]This mod affects save games.[/b] Once one of these shapes is on your map, the save will not load without the mod.
[*][b]Start a new save.[/b] Shape patches are generated with the world.
[*]Requires Shapez Shifter.
[/list]

Bugs and requests: https://github.com/QuinnBast/Shapez2-Mods/issues
Licensed under Apache 2.0."
    "changenote" "${CHANGE_NOTE}"
}
